# HTTP examples for module 17-graphql-websocket. Run them from IntelliJ IDEA / VS Code (REST Client).
# Start the lesson first: ./mvnw -pl modules/17-graphql-websocket/lesson spring-boot:run
# A browser IDE for the same queries: http://localhost:8080/graphiql

### 3.2 Query — the client chooses the fields
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "{ books { isbn title price } }"}

### 3.3 Nested fields: author (@BatchMapping) and reviews (@SchemaMapping)
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "query($isbn: ID!) { book(isbn: $isbn) { title author { name } reviews { stars text } } }",
 "variables": {"isbn": "9780134685991"}}

### 3.4 Mutation
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "mutation($input: ReviewInput!) { addReview(input: $input) { id stars text } }",
 "variables": {"input": {"isbn": "9781449373320", "stars": 5, "text": "Eye-opening."}}}

### 3.4 Mutation with an error (HTTP 200, the error is in the "errors" array)
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "mutation($input: ReviewInput!) { addReview(input: $input) { id } }",
 "variables": {"input": {"isbn": "9781449373320", "stars": 6, "text": "Too good."}}}

### 3.6 Change a price — open http://localhost:8080/prices.html first to see the push
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/9780321336781/price
Content-Type: application/json

{"price": 49.90}

### 3.6 Unknown book → 404 ProblemDetail
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/0000000000000/price
Content-Type: application/json

{"price": 10.00}
